  "holistic_F_N": 2,
  "holistic_F_H": -2,
  "section_notes": "Final rules are strict on incident reporting and mandatory recall at 8/100k, but S2 is weakened for Northwind: the 55°C failure cap is 8% (not 5%) and exceeding it triggers review/corrective action rather than automatic market exclusion. The 6-year retrofit deadline satisfies NW-2, and the 36-month suppression start satisfies HC-2, while per-model results go to purchasers and regulators but not the general public. The recall trigger at 8/100k with no transition means Halcyon's Ember 8 (9.9) would trigger recall, whereas Northwind's Hearth 10 (6.2) would not."
